---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";

const lreGuides = [
  {
    title: "Lucius -- Next LRE Event",
    description: "Coming July 26",
    href: "/lre/lucius",
    thumbnail: "/images/web/lucius-lre.webp",
  },
  {
    title: "Uthar LRE Guide",
    description: "Next to occur after Lucius, unless a new LRE is announced",
    href: "/lre/uthar",
    thumbnail: "/images/web/uthar-lre.webp",
  },
  {
    title: "Farsight LRE Guide",
    description: "Last seen June 2026, his 3rd event date is TBD",
    href: "/lre/farsight",
    thumbnail: "/images/web/farsight-lre.webp",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Legendary Release Events | Terminus Maximus Infographics"
  description="Legendary Release Event guides for unlock planning, team building, and event requirements."
  image="/images/web/lre.webp"
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Legendary Release Events</h1>
      <p>Guides for unlock planning, team building, and event requirements.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>LRE Guides</h2>

      <div class="card-grid">
        {lreGuides.map((guide) => (
          <a class="card" href={guide.href}>
            <div class="card-image-wrap">
              <img
                src={guide.thumbnail}
                alt={`${guide.title} preview`}
                class="card-image"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>

            <h3>{guide.title}</h3>
            <p>{guide.description}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>LRE Basics</h2>

      <div class="markdown-content">
        <h3>Legendary Release Events Are Roster Checks</h3>

        <p>
          Legendary Release Events are some of the most demanding events in Tacticus.
          The goal is simple: earn enough points to unlock the featured Legendary character.
        </p>

        <p>
          The challenge is that you are not clearing one normal campaign path. LREs are split
          across multiple tracks, each with its own battles, restrictions, and scoring requirements.
        </p>

        <p>
          Progress carries over between appearances, so every clear matters even if you will not
          unlock the character in a single event.
        </p>

        <h3>Requirements Drive the Strategy</h3>

        <p>
          Most LRE planning comes down to matching the right characters to the right requirements.
          A good team is not always your five strongest characters.
        </p>

        <p>Common requirements include things like:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Faction restrictions</li>
          <li>Damage types</li>
          <li>Traits and keywords</li>
          <li>Rarity limits</li>
          <li>Survival or no-summon conditions</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The best teams often cover multiple requirements at once while still having enough damage,
          healing, summons, or durability to survive deeper stages.
        </p>

        <h3>Plan Around the Roster You Actually Have</h3>

        <p>
          It is easy to look at an ideal LRE team and feel like you are missing half the pieces.
          That is normal.
        </p>

        <p>
          Instead of chasing every perfect lineup, focus on characters that solve multiple problems:
          durable tanks, reliable healers, reusable damage dealers, summoners, and supports that show
          up across more than one event.
        </p>

        <p>
          A flexible roster will carry you farther than one narrow team built for a single requirement.
        </p>

        <h3>Use These Guides as a Planning Tool</h3>

        <p>
          The goal of these LRE guides is to make the event easier to understand before you spend
          resources. Use them to compare tracks, spot useful characters, and identify which requirements
          your account is already close to covering.
        </p>

        <p>
          You do not need to perfect every battle. Focus on steady progress, smart investment, and
          building characters that will keep paying off in future Legendary Release Events.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    background-color: #121212;
    color: #f5f5f5;
    font-family: 'Lexend', sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: #cccccc;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    color: #d4af37;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .content-section {
    background: #1e1e1e;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .markdown-content {
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .markdown-content h3 {
    color: #f5f5f5;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .markdown-content h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .markdown-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .markdown-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .markdown-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .markdown-content a {
    color: #d4af37;
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 320px));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-content: start;
  }

  .card {
    background: #1e1e1e;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .card:hover,
  .card:focus-visible {
    border-color: #d4af37;
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    outline: none;
  }

  .card-image-wrap {
    width: 100%;
    height: 120px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: #121212;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .card-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    object-position: top;
    display: block;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: #d4af37;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .card p {
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    main {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    section {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .card {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .card-image-wrap {
      height: 110px;
    }
  }
</style>